I had been playing my current Wiz-Fem-Elf-Cha *extremely* carefully.
Two things had been making her life difficult, one my fault, the other
not. Not my fault is NO altars in first 10 levels of main dungeon
(Oracle is on DL 9), and Minetown altar is of different alignment. My
fault is that early on (during first visit to Minetown, IIRC) I put a
bag of tricks into BoH. I remembered about wands of cancellation and
BoH; did not remember that BoT would do same thing. So from then on I
was stuck carrying heavy loads. At least I had a regular sack, so did
not have to worry about inventory being full ALSO.

Well, earlier today I killed a white unicorn while in main dungeon (DL
7) and was determined to get it to the altar. My ring of teleport
control is always on, I leash my pet green dragon, drop the bag to
lessen the weight, engrave Elbereth with a fire wand to keep various
interlopers from stealing the bag, lift the unicorn corpse. "You can
barely move a span with that load!" Quaff a levitation potion -- still
Stressed. Confuse myself and read teleportation scroll, intending to go
to DL 4 and the Mines entrance. Oops!

Sometimes reading scrolls of teleportation while confused sends you to
a random level -- in my case, one level down. Nothing to do now but
drop the corpse and let the dragon eat it. On top of that I found
unable to descend -- another mistake. I thought you can stop levitating
at will with any non-cursed potion, while it is only true for blessed
ones. So I probably would not have gotten the corpse to the altar in
time anyway. Sigh.

I wait for the potion to expire, take the dragon one level down to
Oracle and bone pile... Where is my BAG!? Leave the dragon, quickly get
up to DL 7 (teleportitis+control is wonderful)... and no bag.

Telepathy shows a nymph and an orc. Kill both, but neither one has the
bag. Quaff a PoOD -- no luck. Nothing critical in it -- gold, gems, a
pile of 0-charge wands, and an uncursed luckstone (the blessed one is
in my inventory), -- but the bag itself is important! Now I am stuck
with a constantly full inventory, can not pick anything without
dropping something else. It's annoying.

Now that I think of it, I just picked up some unknown wands in Sokoban.
With luck, one of them will be polymorph, and I will be able to
polypile some tools. BTW, my Sleep spell ran out (20,000 turns) just as
I was putting the last boulders into topmost Sokoban level. The zoo is
tougher than usual, so me and my dragon trekked down Sokoban, up to DL
4, into the Mines, and down to Minetown where my spellbooks are
stashed. Oh, for a BoH!



